{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788113684796213787,"compiled_state":{"alias":"unsavoury-desertic-ant","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"fc22e520a34f44335c7a00ede599b10f43ce9e3943bc981ea3498a39d549cee4","event_uuid":"fbc61340-c0eb-4ecf-bbdf-88b7b8335fd2","position":{"commit_sha":"f330507e8738fbf3a083d001960a044658481358","position":"1788111163572289990-fbc61340-c0eb-4ecf-bbdf-88b7b8335fd2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"9198ac48db47297751b1ab1af7167368be7dd17ab1043b6be81b3a17f9a62dad","event_uuid":"90801151-20df-48ad-8bba-7e027aff0362","position":{"commit_sha":"5e61f95538507e5deaeb90277fdab4d63a653f32","position":"1788111179488067591-90801151-20df-48ad-8bba-7e027aff0362"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"50b24f3ec841871987a971ccd0d2ad33416014cebf28f8eefe11e2dd8c51db49","event_uuid":"de103d67-8258-4970-b2f1-e7cab17c1350","position":{"commit_sha":"a82a8a3049babf1b761979fb23a7e2abf694190a","position":"1788111184433372853-de103d67-8258-4970-b2f1-e7cab17c1350"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788111163572289990,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"90801151-20df-48ad-8bba-7e027aff0362","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"1f35-74fc-47a0-4d71"},{"link_uuid":"de103d67-8258-4970-b2f1-e7cab17c1350","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"eb64-844b-ab7a-4915"}],"description":"## Context\n\nSplit from `floating-chromium-leafwing` (1f35-74fc-47a0-4d71), Decision 6 (operator-approved 2026-08-30). That bug is being resolved now by bounding `anthropic` in `pyproject.toml` (portable, eb64-free) so the mirror-sweep legs stop floating to `anthropic==1.2.0`, whose client vendors `httpx2` and rejects a stdlib `httpx.AsyncClient`. **This ticket carries the long-term fix:** adapt rebar's Anthropic provider seam so it works against the httpx2 `http_client` contract, so the cap 1f35 adds can be lifted.\n\n## Why this is deferred (blocked_by eb64)\n\nThe change touches `src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py:_build_retrying_anthropic_provider`, which is inside epic `financial-stoneware-brant` (eb64-844b-ab7a-4915) declared scope, and collides directly with the in-flight anthropic-backoff work (254e) — which enhances that same retrying provider by passing a custom `httpx.AsyncClient`, exactly the seam this change must rework. Doing both concurrently would conflict. Sequence this AFTER eb64 lands and AFTER 254e, and **preserve 254e's jitter + Retry-After backoff semantics** (re-express them on the httpx2 transport rather than dropping them).\n\n## Plan\n\n- Detect the installed anthropic SDK's expected `http_client` type and construct the provider accordingly: a stdlib `httpx.AsyncClient` for pre-httpx2 SDKs, the vendored `httpx2` client for httpx2 SDKs — OR stop passing a custom client and re-implement retry/backoff via the SDK's supported transport/retry hook.\n- Once the seam supports httpx2, lift or widen the `anthropic` upper bound that 1f35 added to `pyproject.toml`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The Anthropic provider constructs without `TypeError` against an anthropic SDK that vendors httpx2 (the `1.2.0` line and later) AND against the currently-pinned pre-httpx2 SDK.\n- [ ] 254e's retry/backoff behavior (jitter + Retry-After) is preserved and covered by tests.\n- [ ] The `anthropic` upper bound introduced for 1f35 is lifted or widened once the seam is compatible, and the mirror-sweep legs stay green.\n- [ ] Portable across CI providers / no CI.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","eb64-844b-ab7a-4915"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["llm","packaging","test-portability"],"ticket_id":"2bd6-ff87-d48c-4a65","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Adapt anthropic provider seam to the httpx2 http_client contract (lift the 1f35 cap)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["fbc61340-c0eb-4ecf-bbdf-88b7b8335fd2","90801151-20df-48ad-8bba-7e027aff0362","de103d67-8258-4970-b2f1-e7cab17c1350"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788113684796213787,"uuid":"ace13f2c-5a6c-4e4c-beea-41d011d85953"}